    "updated_at": "2026-11-09T18:25:41Z",
    "body": "**Judgement calls for the maintainer** (stays a draft until the Tormach output has a PathPilot Hub run):\n1. **Rapids aren't protected.** Only feeds become protected moves; safe-plane rapids, including the drop to the approach height, stay G0. Protecting them would make every cycle much slower.\n2. **A script without `onProbeGuard` is refused by name**, even if it has no probing, so a motion is never silently dropped. Once this merges, the Haas, Mazak and Siemens posts in #360 need the hook.\n3. **Each dialect alarms its own way.** Fanuc writes `#3000=3` with one `IF` per moving axis. Tormach writes `MSG` + `M2`, matching #376's out-of-tolerance pattern.\n4. **The protected moves are worked out from the touches**, not stored on the toolpath, so the project format doesn't change.\n5. **Overlap with #376:** the Tormach probe goldens will need regenerating after #376 lands (it fixes `S0 M3` and adds the touches).",
