    "updated_at": "2026-11-09T19:56:06Z",
    "body": "**PathPilot Hub check passed** (770MX sim, PathPilot v2.14.4), run by the contributor on this PR's Tormach output. The probe was renumbered T7 → T99, the Hub's default probe slot; only the `T`/`H` words changed.\n\n- The program ran with no G-code warnings or errors: cycle time 00:00:38, last line 38, ends on `M30`.\n- All four positioning feeds ran as `G38.3` at F300: down to Z15 and back up to Z50 at (-7, 5), then at (5, -7). The status line shows `G38.3` active mid-move.\n- No trip on positioning: \"PROBE HIT ON POSITIONING\" never appeared, so each `o500x if [#5070 EQ 1]` check read \"not tripped\" and skipped its `M2`.\n\n**Not exercised:** the tripped branch, because the Hub sim has no way to trip the probe input while a program runs. That branch (`MSG` then `M2`) is for the maintainer to review by reading it.\n\n**Merge order:** the probe section still posts `S0 M3` after the tool change. That comes from the Tormach post's shared spindle preamble on main, and #523 fixes it in every mill post. Please merge the #523 fix first; this branch then takes `git merge origin/main`, so a probe section posts no spindle start.\n\nMarking ready for review.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
