    "body": "Re the review's compensation note: no change needed. `tormach.cps` refuses control cutter compensation outright. Any G41/G42 request posts the message \"control cutter compensation (G41/G42) is not supported by this post\" (line 186). Every section preamble also writes `G40` (line 256). So no Tormach section, the probe's `onProbeGuard` included, can run with compensation engaged, which is the state Fanuc's `compRefuse` guards against. LinuxCNC would also refuse a `G38.x` under G41/G42 by itself.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
